        <item>
            <title>0.4.3</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:06:16 -0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/siplay01/whiskers-releases</link>
            <sparkle:version>0.4.3</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Whiskers 0.4.3</h2><p>New app icon: a microphone with whiskers.<br><br>Record a meeting: Start Meeting Recording before a call (Slack, Zoom, Meet). Whiskers records your mic and the Mac's sound as two tracks, and when you stop, writes a report with who spoke, labeled You and Other 1, Other 2. The first time, macOS asks for Screen & System Audio Recording permission.<br><br>More reliable dictation:<br>- A recording is no longer lost. If nothing was recognized or transcription failed, the recording stays in History with Re-transcribe.<br>- Plugging in or removing headphones while you hold the key no longer stops the recording.<br>- In a password field, Whiskers does not paste. It copies the text and tells you why.<br>- If the text did not land in a text field, Whiskers says so and leaves it on the clipboard.<br>- Clipboard managers no longer keep your dictations, and your previous clipboard comes back after 1.5 seconds, so slow apps paste the right text.<br>- History shows the original text next to the cleaned one.<br>- Speech models are pinned to a fixed version and checked after download.<br><br>The app's internal name changed, so macOS asks once more for Accessibility and Microphone access.</p>
]]></description>
